@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/draw#> .
@prefix draw: <http://example.org/orexis/draw#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix speech: <http://example.org/orexis/speech#> .
@prefix coordination: <http://example.org/orexis/coordination#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph ;    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is
    owl:imports <actions.ttl> , <rules.ttl> , <shapes.ttl> .

#  THE DRAW, A DOMAIN.
#  A fair coin between two agents with no third party and no shared store, by commit and reveal (Blum): each
#  COMMITS to a number by saying its hash, and once it has heard the peer's commitment REVEALS the number; each
#  checks the peer's reveal against the peer's commitment, and both compute the winner from the two numbers.
#  What it decides is a conflict of the coordination package's (agent/coordination/), and it says the outcome
#  in that package's word, `coordination:wonBy`, so the package reads who goes first and names no domain; a
#  world imports this to have its agents draw, and could import another way of deciding instead
#  (two-agents-that-want-one-resource-ask-each-other-and-draw-lots-for-it, knowledge/domain/draw/draw.md).
#
#  THE NUMBERS. An agent's number for a draw is the hash of the secret it minted (`coordination:secret`) and the
#  draw's name; its commitment the hash of the draw's name and its number; the winner the first hex digit of the
#  hash of the draw's name and both numbers, the lower-named agent's first: odd, the lower-named agent goes
#  first, even the other. The draw's name binds the pair, the conflict and the round, so nothing from another
#  draw can be replayed into this one; no arithmetic, since the engine's is a known trap.
#  No Python: the protocol is the documents, the actions and the rules.

#################  What is said  #################

:CommitmentGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf speech:StatementGraph ; rdfs:label "Commitment graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "A graph holding one commitment, as it was said: a statement." .

:RevealGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf speech:StatementGraph ; rdfs:label "Reveal graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "A graph holding one reveal, as it was said: a statement." .

:Commitment a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Commitment" ;
    rdfs:comment "What an agent says first in a draw: the hash of the draw's name and its number, binding it to a number it has not shown (knowledge/domain/draw/draw.md)." .

:Reveal a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Reveal" ;
    rdfs:comment "What an agent says once it has heard the peer's commitment: its number, which a reveal must hash, with the draw's name, to the commitment the same agent said, or it is refused (knowledge/domain/draw/draw.md)." .

:of a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "of" ;
    rdfs:comment "The draw a commitment or a reveal is of: `coordination:draw` of a conflict's present round." .

:by a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range orexis:Agent ; rdfs:label "by" ;
    rdfs:comment "Who said the commitment or the reveal." .

:about a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range coordination:Conflict ; rdfs:label "about" ;
    rdfs:comment "The conflict the draw decides, said so the peer knows which conflict, and in which round, it is drawing." .

:round a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ; rdfs:label "round" ;
    rdfs:comment "The round of the conflict the draw is of, said so a peer behind it is brought to it." .

:hash a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain :Commitment ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:label "hash" ;
    rdfs:comment "The hash a commitment binds its sayer to." .

:number a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain :Reveal ; rdfs:range xsd:string ; rdfs:label "number" ;
    rdfs:comment "The number a reveal shows." .

:committedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range orexis:Agent ; rdfs:label "committed by" ;
    rdfs:comment "An agent whose commitment to a draw the agent believes it said: concluded of a commitment, the agent's own or a peer's." .

:revealedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range orexis:Agent ; rdfs:label "revealed by" ;
    rdfs:comment "An agent whose reveal of a draw the agent believes it said." .

:peer a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range orexis:Agent ; rdfs:label "peer" ;
    rdfs:comment "Whom a commitment or a reveal is taken with: the peer every standing conflict it is taken over is with, the one parameter both actions take." .
